# The object of the definition is a parameter of a function that code nobody sees may call: the object may be its own, so what the descriptor holds under `value` goes out of sight; the descriptor itself is only read by the built-in and stays. L0 = what is laid, L2 = the descriptor.
# RUN: link layouts mechanisms=all
# CHECK: layout L0 changes=[IsFrozen, GainsProperty, LosesProperty, ChangesPrototype, GetsAccessor]
# CHECK: layout L2 changes=[] stays-with-compiled-code
